' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. A dedicated REGRESSION fixture for
' a real, genuine bug found while verifying the Random.* host-function
' bridge (fission/tests/native_programs/host_bridge_random.abas): ANY
' integer literal outside the signed 32-bit range (roughly +/- 2.1
' billion) was silently corrupted by this backend's own operand-loading
' path, because the only real x86-64 immediate-to-register/immediate-to-
' memory MOV encoding (`MOV r/m64, imm32`) always sign-extends its imm32
' operand into the 64-bit destination -- a real ISA constraint, not a
' choice this backend made. Confirmed directly: `PRINT 4294967295` used
' to silently print `-1`, and `Random.Integer(0, 4294967295, handle)`
' used to CRASH the compiled binary outright with SIGFPE (a downstream
' divide-by-zero once the corrupted "width" argument reached
' `arco_host_random_integer`'s own bounded-rejection loop).
'
' Fixed for real, not worked around: a register destination has a REAL,
' correct full-width encoding (REX.W + B8+rd io, `MOV r64, imm64`, no
' sign-extension at all -- fission/amir/x86_64_assembler.abas's own `mov`
' handling now uses it whenever the immediate does not fit in a signed
' 32-bit value), and the one direct immediate-to-MEMORY store this
' backend's own codegen ever emitted (a bare `Const` instruction's own
' stack-slot initialization, fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas) is now routed
' through that same real register-destination encoding first (load into a
' scratch register, then store the register to memory -- the exact same
' two-step pattern every OTHER value in this whole file already uses, not
' a special case).
'
' Exercises: a bare PRINT of a large positive/negative literal, a variable
' assignment (the exact `Const`-instruction code path that crashed),
' arithmetic on a large literal, and the large-literal-as-host-bridge-
' argument shape that originally crashed with SIGFPE.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
PRINT 4294967295
PRINT -4294967296
PRINT 2147483647
PRINT 2147483648
PRINT -2147483648
PRINT -2147483649

x = 4294967295
PRINT x

y = x + 1
PRINT y

z = x - 4294967295
PRINT z

h = Random.Create(100)
PRINT Random.Integer(0, 4294967295, h)
